  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records establish that chemical short-range order and temperature-dependent ordering are important in W-Ta-Cr-V and closely related W-Ta-Cr-V-Hf refractory alloys, especially R2, R4, and R10. R1 and R16 also show relevant atomistic or first-principles treatment of finite-temperature structural and electronic effects. However, none describes an MTP or comparable machine-learning potential replacing an EAM reference for the liquid, nor FEP replacing thermodynamic integration by exploiting low MTP–DFT energy-difference variance. They also do not identify the DOS-gap electronic Gibbs contribution to melting. Thus the literature points toward including SRO and finite-temperature electronic physics, but the specific MTP-plus-FEP acceleration strategy would require a substantial new idea."
